llvm-cvpack pack keeps one base pack: objects only reference records that the
base holds and never another pack, the rest stays in the objects, and the run
rebases by itself when the base no longer fits the inputs. The inputs are the
clang-generated objects of cvpacks-pack-shared.test.

An object staged unchanged lists no pack: "packs": [] only matches the entry of
such an object.

RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t/orig %t/work
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-src-a.yaml -o %t/orig/a.obj
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-src-b.yaml -o %t/orig/b.obj
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-src-c.yaml -o %t/orig/c.obj
RUN: yaml2obj %S/Inputs/cvpacks-src-d.yaml -o %t/orig/d.obj

Without a pack, the first run writes the base.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --pack-path=%t/packs \
RUN:   --out-dir=%t/stage1 %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MANIFEST1 < %t/stage1/cvpacks.json
MANIFEST1-NOT:  "packs": []
MANIFEST1:      "new_packs": [
MANIFEST1-NEXT:   "[[BASE:[0-9a-f]+]]"
MANIFEST1-NEXT: ],
MANIFEST1-NEXT: "base": "[[BASE]]"

c.obj and d.obj share Segment, which the base lacks: it stays in them, and no
pack is written. The manifest says how far the base is from a rebase: the
inputs use all of it, and a rebase would pack more.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --auto-rebase=no \
RUN:   --pack-path=%t/packs --out-dir=%t/stage2 %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj \
RUN:   %t/orig/c.obj %t/orig/d.obj
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MANIFEST2 < %t/stage2/cvpacks.json
MANIFEST2-NOT:  "packs": []
MANIFEST2:      "new_packs": [],
MANIFEST2-NEXT: "base": "{{[0-9a-f]+}}",
MANIFEST2-NEXT: "base_bytes": [[BYTES:[1-9][0-9]*]],
MANIFEST2-NEXT: "base_used_bytes": [[BYTES]],
MANIFEST2-NEXT: "missing_bytes": {{[1-9][0-9]*}}
RUN: %python -c "import glob; print(len(glob.glob(r'%t/packs/*.cvp')))" \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONEPACK
ONEPACK: {{^}}1{{$}}

Objects packed against the base materialize back to their original bytes, and
link to the same PDB as the originals. The packs are in a directory of their
own, which the links search as they search for a library.
RUN: llvm-cvpack materialize --pack-path=%t/packs %t/stage2/c.obj -o %t/c.restored.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig/c.obj %t/c.restored.obj
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; [shutil.copyfile(r'%t/orig/' + f, r'%t/work/' + f) for f in ('a.obj', 'b.obj', 'c.obj', 'd.obj')]"
RUN: lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug /timestamp:0 /pdbaltpath:base.pdb \
RUN:   /libpath:%t/packs /pdb:%t/work/out.pdb /out:%t/work/out.dll \
RUN:   %t/work/a.obj %t/work/b.obj %t/work/c.obj %t/work/d.obj
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; shutil.copyfile(r'%t/work/out.pdb', r'%t/orig.pdb')"
RUN: %python -c "import shutil; [shutil.copyfile(r'%t/stage2/' + f, r'%t/work/' + f) for f in ('a.obj', 'b.obj', 'c.obj', 'd.obj')]"
RUN: lld-link /noentry /dll /nodefaultlib /debug /timestamp:0 /pdbaltpath:base.pdb \
RUN:   /libpath:%t/packs /pdb:%t/work/out.pdb /out:%t/work/out.dll \
RUN:   %t/work/a.obj %t/work/b.obj %t/work/c.obj %t/work/d.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/orig.pdb %t/work/out.pdb

With the default thresholds the missing bytes are over 25% of the base: the
run rebases, and --prune deletes the previous base.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --prune \
RUN:   --pack-path=%t/packs --out-dir=%t/stage3 %t/orig/a.obj %t/orig/b.obj \
RUN:   %t/orig/c.obj %t/orig/d.obj
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=MANIFEST3 < %t/stage3/cvpacks.json
MANIFEST3-NOT:  "packs": []
MANIFEST3:      "new_packs": [
MANIFEST3-NEXT:   "[[NEW:[0-9a-f]+]]"
MANIFEST3-NEXT: ],
MANIFEST3-NEXT: "base": "[[NEW]]",
MANIFEST3-NEXT: "rebased_because": "{{[0-9]+}} bytes that a rebase would pack are not in the base, over 25% of it"
RUN: %python -c "import glob; print(len(glob.glob(r'%t/packs/*.cvp')))" \
RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=ONEPACK

Restored objects packed against the base are staged unchanged, count towards
its use, and the other inputs stage as before.
RUN: llvm-cvpack pack --pack-path=%t/packs \
RUN:   --out-dir=%t/stage4 %t/stage3/a.obj %t/stage3/b.obj %t/stage3/c.obj \
RUN:   %t/orig/d.obj
RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=HITS < %t/stage4/cvpacks.json
HITS-NOT:  "packs": []
HITS:      "new_packs": [],
HITS-NEXT: "base": "{{[0-9a-f]+}}",
HITS-NEXT: "base_bytes": [[BYTES4:[1-9][0-9]*]],
HITS-NEXT: "base_used_bytes": [[BYTES4]],
HITS-NEXT: "missing_bytes": 0
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage3/a.obj %t/stage4/a.obj
RUN: %python %S/Inputs/check-files-equal.py %t/stage3/d.obj %t/stage4/d.obj

RUN: not llvm-cvpack pack --auto-rebase=25 --pack-path=%t/packs \
RUN:   --out-dir=%t/stage5 %t/orig/a.obj 2>&1 | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=BADARG
BADARG: --auto-rebase: expected <missing>,<used> percentages or 'no', got 25
